From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:27:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, pipeline library shaders cached
 and counted

With MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, a pipeline library's shader now
serializes into pipeline caches (kk_gpl_serialize) instead of being
left out. Its blob holds what a link compiles it with: the NIR, the
create flags, the robustness state, its set layouts (what compiling
reads of them: bindings' types, sizes, offsets and strides, dynamic
buffer indices), the embedded samplers, the push constant range, the
sample shading state and the view mask; and the vertex and fragment
shaders compiled on their own, with their MSL and what links check of
them, and the reasons a source could not be compiled on its own, by
name. Deserializing it (kk_gpl_deserialize) builds their Metal
libraries again from that MSL, and the empty fragment shader with a
vertex shader as at compile. A source whose reason may not hold in
another run (out of memory, a failed Metal library build) or whose set
layout has a Y'CbCr conversion is not serialized. The blob starts with
a magic word where a whole pipeline's starts with its stage, then a
version: a blob of another version is refused rather than read, and the
cache key marker is bumped to kk-gpl-separate-v4.

The vertex and fragment shaders compiled on their own keep their MSL
packed, as other shaders do, and links inflate a copy. Under
MESA_KK_DEBUG=memory they count as shaders, and each device counts its
library shaders, the shaders compiled on their own (the empty fragment
shader's too), their Metal libraries and its links: on the [kk-mem]
line ("| gpl sources= shaders= libraries= links=") and, when the device
goes, before and after it releases its own ("[kk-mem] gpl device
finish").

MESA_KK_DEBUG=compile logs "[kk-compile] link totals links= separate=
separate-vertex= full= failed= fallbacks=<reason>:<count>,..." every 64
links and when the device goes. Fallbacks are counted by the reason's
text.

A draw whose link key, in the mode of the link bound last, and colour
attachment count are those of that link uses it without the fragment
side's checks and the pair's fallback lookup: what they read is in the
key. The empty fragment shader is read without a lock once compiled.

Nothing changes without the flag, and no MSL changes with it.

Linear: PLA-424
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-21-kk-gpl-host.md
Offered-upstream: not yet
